h sites\nCampus tours\nCampus tours\nVirtual tours\nEnhance your employability\nEnhance your employability\nGlobal experiences\nEntrepreneurship\nLeadership and representation\nResearch opportunities\nInternships\nMentoring\nVolunteering\nWhy choose UQ\nInformation and resources\nInformation and resources\nFor international students\nFor high school students\nFor high school students\nGlossary of terms\nYoung Achievers Program\nYoung Achievers Program\nHow to apply\nHow to apply\nCheck your eligibility\nReview commitments\nReview key dates\nSubmit your application\nYoung ChangeMakers Program\nYoung ChangeMakers Program\nHow to apply\nBecome a student mentor\nCareer Pulse Hub\nCareer Pulse Hub\nSustainability careers\nInnovation careers\nTechnology careers\nLeadership careers\nHuman connection careers\nFor under-represented groups\nFor non-school leavers\nFor Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students\nFor Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander students\nInspireU\nInspireU\nInspireU Discover (Years 7-9)\nInspireU Explore (Years 10-12)\nInspireU Extend (Years 10-12)\nInspireU Scholars (Years 11-12)\nTertiary Experience Day\nFor teachers and guidance counsellors\nFor teachers and guidance counsellors\nHigh school activities\nHigh school activities\nHigh school visits\nCareer expos\nUQ school event calendar\nEvents for career advisers\nRequest a school presentation\nRequest a campus tour\nInternational regional managers\nFor parents and guardians\nFor study abroad and exchange students\nFor PhD and research degree students\nFor current students\nEvents\nStories\nContact\nContact\nSend us an enquiry\nApplication help and contact\nFind an agent near you\nStudy\nResearch\nPartners and community\nAbout\nUQ home\nNews\nEvents\nGive\nContact\nSearch term\nUQ home\nNews\nEvents\nGive\nContact\nUQ home\nStudy\nAdmissions\nPhD, MPhil and professional doctorate\nApplication dates\nI'm a domestic student\nI'm an international student\nApplication dates\nUnderstand when you need to apply by for entry into a research program.\nTo apply, you will need to submit:\nan initial expression of interest (EOI), to ensure a supervisor will support your research\na final application, if invited after the supervisor reviews your EOI.\nThe deadlines to submit your EOI or final application will depend on whether you\u2019re applying for a UQ scholarship or project with a specific closing date.\nGenerally, you will need to apply at least 6 months before starting at UQ to allow enough time for your Australian student visa to be processed. Plan for visa processing to take approximately 12 weeks. You must receive an offer before you can apply for a visa.\nYour situation\nApplication dates\nYou want to be considered for a project\nEOI: Submit by the date listed on the project page.\nFinal application: If invited, submit as soon as possible.\nAllow up to 12 weeks from the EOI closing date to receive the outcome of your final application.\nYou want to be considered for our major living stipend scholarship: Graduate Research School Scholarships (UQGRSS) \u2013 includes Research Training Program (RTP)\nEOI: Submit by the date listed on the scholarship page.\nFinal application: If invited, submit by the date listed on the scholarship page.\nCheck the scholarship page for offer dates.\nYou want to be considered for a UQ scholarship with a specific closing date.\nEOI: Submit as early as possible.\nFinal application: If invited, submit by the date listed on the scholarship page.\nAllow up to 12 weeks from the application closing date listed on the scholarship page to receive the outcome of your final application.\nYou want to be considered for a UQ scholarship that does not have a specific closing date.\nEOI: Submit as early as possible.\nFinal application: If invited, submit as soon as possible.\nTo be eligible to start in a particular research quarter, you will need to submit your final application by the following dates:\nRQ 1 (January): 30 September\nRQ 2 (April): 31 December\nRQ 3 (July): 31 March\nRQ 4 (October): 30 June.\nRQ 1 (January): 30 June\nRQ 2 (April): 30 September\nRQ 3 (July): 31 December\nRQ 4 (October): 31 March.\nAllow up to 12 weeks from the application closing date to receive the outcome of your final application.\nYou do not want to be considered for a UQ scholarship or project.\nEOI: Submit as early as possible.\nFinal application: If invited, submit as soon as possible.\nTo be eligible to start in a particular research quarter, you will need to submit your final application by the following dates:\nRQ 1 (January): 30 September\nRQ 2 (April): 31 December\nRQ 3 (July): 31 March\nRQ 4 (October): 30 June.\nRQ 1 (January): 30 June\nRQ 2 (April): 30 September\nRQ 3 (July): 31 December\nRQ 4 (October): 31 March.\nAllow up to 12 weeks from the application closing date to receive the outcome of your final application.\nIf you are applying for external scholarships or sponsorship, you will also need to meet any deadlines for those.\nResearch quarter key dates\nOur research academic year is divided into 4 research quarters. See key dates for starting your program, paying fees and finalising enrolment.\nSee research quarter key dates\nUQ acknowledges the Traditional Owners and their custodianship of the lands on which UQ is situated. Reconciliation at UQ\nMedia\nMedia team contacts\nFind a subject matter expert\nUQ News\nWorking with us\nCareers and job search\nStrategic Plan\nStaff Intranet\nIT support\nCurrent students\nmy.UQ\nPrograms and courses\nAcademic calendar\nStudent support\nIT support\nLibrary\nLibrary\nStudy and learning support\nResearch and publish\nVisit\nContact\nContact UQ\nMake a complaint\nFaculties, schools, institutes and centres\nDivisions and departments\nCampuses, maps and transport\nMedia\nMedia team contacts\nFind a subject matter expert\nUQ News\nWorking with us\nCareers and job search\nStrategic Plan\nStaff Intranet\nIT support\nCurrent students\nmy.UQ\nPrograms and courses\nAcademic ca